  "subject": {
    "id": "one-source-of-truth-for-a-records-modality",
    "type": "DOCUMENT"
  },
  "summary": "A record's assertion_modality must be one its formalizing assertion carries; the unbound-range refusal names the range and the five that bind; the skill says what a name is.",
  "why": "Twenty of run-09's 212 source-asserted records carried a modality no assertion behind them carries, MEASURED in the capture and STATED on the record twelve times, because the record's modality was a second copy written against the clause where the capture tagged the sentence. Only the assertion carries evidence, so the adapter now refuses a record whose assertion_modality no assertion formalizing its properties path carries, typed MODALITY_NOT_ASSERTED and aggregated with the other derivation defects. Decision 19 records it and names the removal it defers. Two returns that cost a first attempt each are message and prose, not rules: INVALID_RANGE now names the range that failed to bind and the five seed scalars that do, and the skill's claim that every LinkML built-in loads is corrected to the inspector, where it is true, against the compiler, where date and uri refuse; and the skill now says an entity's name is the form the source uses to refer to it. The validated-contract artifact pins a producer digest over five pipeline files, elaborate.py among them, so the inspection-note change fixture carries a recomputed ledger head."
}
